(Glossary \(first sheet\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (A leg: The portion of a call between the contact and NiCE CXone. On an inbound call it is ingress.) Tj
T* (B leg: The portion of a call between NiCE CXone and the agent. A transfer adds a second B leg.) Tj
T* (PSTN: On the connectivity page, phone traffic routed by DID or toll-free number.) Tj
T* (DID: Direct Inward Dial. The connectivity page uses it as one of the two PSTN number types.) Tj
T* (TFN: Toll-free number. The preferred path is to make CXone the RespOrg.) Tj
T* (RespOrg: Responsible Organization for a toll-free number. If CXone is the RespOrg, you order more numbers thro) Tj
T* (Voice PoP: The carrier's physical gateway to the PSTN.) Tj
T* (SIP trunk: A virtual PBX-to-carrier connection using a traditional line, VoIP, or a dedicated path such as MPL) Tj
T* (Integrated Softphone: The built-in agent softphone. Nothing to install. It uses WebRTC. It is not the same nam) Tj
T* (WebRTC: The communications technology in the Chrome browser that Integrated Softphone uses.) Tj
T* (Point of contact: The entry, such as a phone number or email address. It is assigned one skill and one script.) Tj
T* (ACD skill: The thing that automates delivery to an agent who can help. A campaign is required when you create ) Tj
T* (Overall priority: The static-delivery page's formula: \(Time   Acceleration\) + Initial Priority. Time is in m) Tj
T* (Proficiency: 1 is best and 20 is worst. Bullseye uses a high-to-low window.) Tj
T* (Bullseye routing: Delivery that tightens or widens proficiency, or uses routing attributes, with actions such ) Tj
T* (REQAGENT: The Studio action that requests an agent. A blank skill uses the point of contact's skill.) Tj
T* (MENU: Stores the contact's choice in a variable. Prompts can be recorded, TTS, or both.) Tj
T* (DNIS: The number dialed. Phone DNIS is configured by Professional Services before the point of contact.) Tj
T* (Digital skill: The inbound digital path since the Summer 2023 change. New routing queues cannot be created.) Tj
T* (Personal Connection: Proactive voice. Acceleration is set to 0 so the contact does not sit in an inbound-style) Tj
T* (CXone WFM: Forecast, schedule, bids, time off, and adherence. The welcome page states a scale up to 10,000 age) Tj
T* (IEX: A different workforce product. Its help is inside the IEX application.) Tj
T* (AHT: On the forecast page, the average time to complete a transaction from start to finish.) Tj
T* (ScreenAgent: Records and monitors the agent's screen. From version 2.1.40, a voice mask stops active screen re) Tj
T* (Hold gap: Hold audio, including hold music, is not recorded. A consultation during hold is recorded.) Tj
T* (Engagement Hub: Brings third-party PABX, ACD, CRM, digital, and dialer data into CXone for Supervisor, Copilot) Tj
T* (Multi-ACD: Real-time recording of a third-party phone system. Versions live in that table, not in the WFM conn) Tj
T* (Autopilot \(Omilia\): The virtual agent for voice and digital. Voice setup needs NiCE. Text needs Digital Expe) Tj
